* Technical concepts\nbehind the 2018 hacks
** Arithmetic
*** Multiplication overflow (BEC batchTransfer)
*** Addition overflow and ecrecover (SMT transferProxy)
*** Unchecked allowance (EDU, BAI)
** Contract control flow
*** Reentrancy via a chosen token (SpankChain)
*** Randomness from block data (Fomo3D airdrop)
*** extcodesize bypass from a constructor
*** Block stuffing (Fomo3D round 1)
** Keys and admin powers
*** Single-key hot wallets (Coincheck, Zaif)
*** Owner mint, burn, withdraw (KICKICO, Bancor)
*** Non-idempotent withdrawals (BitGrail)
** Consensus
*** 51% attacks and confirmations (Bitcoin Gold)
*** Timestamp spoofing (Verge)
*** Duplicate inputs (CVE-2018-17144)
** Front ends and supply chain
*** BGP and DNS hijacks (MyEtherWallet, BlackWallet)
*** Targeted npm payload (event-stream, Copay)
*** Third-party script (StatCounter, Gate.io)
@endmindmap
